            <ArticleTitle>[The role of proximal osteomy of the tibia in the treatment of arthrosis of the knee joint].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The results of heigh tibia osteotomy performed between 1970 and 1975 in 20 cases in the material of the Orthopaedic Department of the &quot;Semmelweis&quot; University Medical School, Budapest, are reported. In 13 cases good--in 6 cases satisfactory results have been obtained. In 1 case the surgical intervention was of no effect. With regard to the explicit pain-relieving effect the operation is recommended by the authors in the treatment of knee arthrosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
